  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>p</mi></math> and <math><mi>q</mi></math> are logical statements, then <math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equivalent to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⇔</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>&#8764;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi></math><br />Hence, the given statement&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology<br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false when <math><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math><mi>q</mi></math> is false</p><p>Hence, not a tautology<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>~</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi></math><br /><math><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>t</mi></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&#8744;</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is a tautology.<br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8743;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is false when <math><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math><mi>q</mi></math> is false</p><p>Hence, not a tautology<br />Also,&nbsp;<math><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&#8660;</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;false when <math><mi>p</mi></math> is true and <math><mi>q</mi></math> is false</p><p>Hence, not a tautology</p>"
  }
}